 ## Current unselected tie-policy proposal
 
 A source-bound direct/mirror tie-policy prototype and optional checkpoint helper are retained at `generators/4512012999bb/workspace/proposals/standalone-be82a6b1da3a8a6d/manifest.json`. The standalone bundle lost its original assignment seed/journal and has no native return contract or completed support tickets. Bundle/member hashes and cached baseline guards were checked statically; all tests/Racket claims remain reviewer-reported. Production source and authority are unchanged; the proposal is not selected, approved or admitted to training.
+
+## Current native alignment candidate
+
+`workspace/parametric/` implements `alignment=match|contrast`: maximize or minimize
+the input-dependent direct/reflected side-color score, with ties direct. The
+default is the byte-exact canonical program. This packet did not contain the
+earlier tie-policy proposal's source, so that unselected record remains separate.
+Canonical generator and reference bytes are unchanged.
+
+Three constructive demonstrations cover strict direct, strict reflected and
+asymmetric ties; independent counts are 3–6 demos and 1–4 queries. Both settings
+share input RNG streams. Ordinary four-query input sizes are 7×10, 16×21, 24×26
+and 30×30; the last has a dense 28×14 crop and produces a 30×16 frame. This is a
+separate grammar extension, not a new production override. No arbitrary rotation
+support is declared.
+
+The causal dependency is guide/crop recovery → first-interior colors and both
+side-match scores → orientation selection and row-preserving insertion. The
+bounded self-review tests ten executable shortcuts using demonstrations only.
+Its scope is finite-rival identifiability, not universal uniqueness or training
+benefit. Odd-center contributions common to both scores are observationally
+irrelevant and are not claimed as an eliminated rival.
+
+Task-local evidence and native manifest bind the candidate. The return includes
+native qualification and a protected counterfactual witness under the main task's
+`checks/` directory. Next owner action: integrate, requalify and explicitly accept
+the exact live source. Reviewer readiness never implies native acceptance or
+training admission.
